### Try the API straight from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension.
### Click "Send Request" above each block. Start Django first (port 8000).

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

### 1. Sign up Rahul
# @name rahul
POST {{base}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rahul", "email": "rahul@example.com", "password": "s3cure-pass-123" }

### 2. Sign up Priya
POST {{base}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Priya", "email": "priya@example.com", "password": "s3cure-pass-123" }

### 3. Log in as Rahul (if he already exists)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "rahul@example.com", "password": "s3cure-pass-123" }

@token = {{login.response.body.access}}

### 4. Balance
GET {{base}}/wallet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Add ₹500
POST {{base}}/wallet/topup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: topup-demo-001

{ "amount": "500" }

### 6. Send ₹200 to Priya. Send this TWICE: the second time you'll get the
###    same response with header "Idempotent-Replayed: true" and no second charge.
POST {{base}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-demo-001

{ "to_email": "priya@example.com", "amount": "200" }

### 7. History
GET {{base}}/transactions?page=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Ask Priya for ₹150
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from_email": "priya@example.com", "amount": "150", "note": "Cab to the airport" }

### 9. Your requests (incoming = others asking you)
GET {{base}}/requests?direction=incoming&status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Pay request #1 (log in as the payer first). Send twice: charged once.
POST {{base}}/requests/1/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: pay-request-demo-001


### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Merchant API
### 11. Create a checkout as a shop's server, using its SECRET key
###     (seed_demo prints the Chai & Co. key once; or get one on the Business page)
@shopKey = sk_test_paste_your_key_here

# @name order
POST {{base}}/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{shopKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": "499.00", "description": "Order #1042", "return_url": "/shop/" }

### 12. Open the checkout_url from the response in your browser and pay.
###     Then look the order up:
GET {{base}}/v1/orders/{{order.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{shopKey}}

### 13. Refund part of it. Send twice: refunded once.
POST {{base}}/v1/orders/{{order.response.body.id}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{shopKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-demo-001

{ "amount": "99.00", "reason": "Late delivery" }

### 14. A risky payment: a brand-new account sending more than ₹5,000 is held (202)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: risky-demo-001

{ "to_email": "priya@example.com", "amount": "6000" }
